  "body": "## Finding Description\n\nIn the `_createCampaign` function, the contract performs minimum reward validation using the gross `newCampaign.amount` before deducting protocol fees:\n```\nif ((newCampaign.amount * HOUR) / newCampaign.duration < rewardTokenMinAmount) \n    revert Errors.CampaignRewardTooLow();\n```\n\nHowever, the actual campaign funding applied to participants is the net amount after fees:\n```\nuint256 campaignAmountMinusFees = _computeFees(newCampaign.campaignType, newCampaign.amount);\nnewCampaign.amount = campaignAmountMinusFees;\n```\n\nThis mismatch allows campaigns that pass the gross amount check to have a net reward per hour below the intended minimum once fees are applied, violating the expected economic guarantees.\n\n## Impact\n\n- Campaigns may distribute rewards below the minimum intended threshold.\n\n- Economic incentives for participants can be weakened, reducing campaign effectiveness and trust in the protocol.\n\n- Protocol rules for minimum funding are bypassable, potentially leading to misaligned campaign rewards.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe contract validates minimum rewards against the gross amount before fees are deducted but uses the net amount after fees for actual distribution.\n\n# Recommended Mitigation\n\n- Perform minimum reward validation on the net amount after fees are computed:\n```\nuint256 campaignAmountMinusFees = _computeFees(newCampaign.campaignType, newCampaign.amount);\nif ((campaignAmountMinusFees * HOUR) / newCampaign.duration < rewardTokenMinAmount)\n    revert Errors.CampaignRewardTooLow();\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "```\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\n\npragma solidity ^0.8.17;\n\nimport { Fixture } from \"../Fixture.t.sol\";\nimport { CampaignParameters } from \"../../contracts/struct/CampaignParameters.sol\";\n\ncontract C4PoC is Fixture {\n    uint256 internal constant maxDistribForOOG = 1e4;\n    uint256 internal constant nbrDistrib = 10;\n    uint32 internal initStartTime;\n    uint32 internal initEndTime;\n    uint32 internal startTime;\n    uint32 internal endTime;\n    uint32 internal numEpoch;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n\n        initStartTime = uint32(block.timestamp);\n        numEpoch = 25;\n        initEndTime = startTime + numEpoch * EPOCH_DURATION;\n\n        vm.prank(governor);\n        creator.setFeeRecipient(dylan);\n\n        vm.startPrank(guardian);\n        address[] memory tokens = new address[](1);\n        uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);\n        tokens[0] = address(angle);\n        amounts[0] = 1e8;\n        creator.setRewardTokenMinAmounts(tokens, amounts);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        angle.mint(address(alice), 1e22);\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        angle.approve(address(creator), type(uint256).max);\n\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n        // Demonstrate: gross amount passes validation but net (after fees) falls below minimum.\n        // Min per-epoch = 1e8 (set in setUp), fee = 10%, duration = 1 hour\n        // Gross = 1e8 passes validation: (1e8 * 3600) / 3600 = 1e8 >= 1e8 ✓\n        // Net = 1e8 * 90% = 9e7 < 1e8 ✗ (but campaign is still accepted)\n\n        uint256 grossAmount = 1e8;\n        \n        CampaignParameters memory campaign = CampaignParameters({\n            campaignId: bytes32(0),\n            creator: alice,\n            rewardToken: address(angle),\n            amount: grossAmount,\n            campaignType: 0,\n            startTimestamp: uint32(block.timestamp + 1),\n            duration: EPOCH_DURATION,\n            campaignData: \"\"\n        });\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        bytes32 campaignId = creator.createCampaign(campaign);\n\n        CampaignParameters memory stored = creator.campaign(campaignId);\n        uint256 storedAmount = stored.amount;\n        \n        // Net after 10% fee: 1e8 * 9e8 / 1e9 = 9e7\n        uint256 expectedNet = (grossAmount * 9e8) / 1e9;\n        assertEq(storedAmount, expectedNet);\n        \n        // Verify: net is below minimum, yet campaign was accepted\n        uint256 minPerEpoch = creator.rewardTokenMinAmounts(address(angle));\n        assertTrue(\n            storedAmount < minPerEpoch,\n            \"Net amount below minimum but campaign was accepted - demonstrates the validation issue\"\n        );\n    }\n\n}\n```",
